    "pathophysiology": "Myxomatous degeneration thickens and lengthens the mitral leaflets and chordae, so one or both leaflets bulge back into the left atrium in systole. Some develop mitral regurgitation.",
    "timeline": {
      "onset": "Usually found incidentally",
      "course": "Mostly benign; a minority progress to significant mitral regurgitation or chordal rupture"
    },
